The build of src/emit/irgen.cc now fails early: after the anonymous namespace, the
IrGenerator method definitions are being parsed as free functions (for example
'bytePointer', 'dynamicPointer', 'storeSlot'), with errors like "'IrGenerator' does
not name a type".

This means namespace jsmm::emit { ... } was closed too early or a stray '}'/
namespace close was inserted before those member definitions.

Current known-good end of file is:
  builder_->SetInsertPoint(endBlock);
}

} // namespace jsmm::emit

and a second copy of emitFormatArray/emitFormatUnion (without IrGenerator::) still
exists after that, which produces the duplicate-definition failures at the end.

Next step:
1) Find the FIRST correctly-placed '} // namespace jsmm::emit' that comes after the
   first emitFormatArray + emitFormatUnion bodies.
2) Truncate the file to end right after that, discarding any later duplicate bodies.
3) Verify the last ~25 lines before the close are the first (correct, IrGenerator::)
   emitFormatArray and emitFormatUnion definitions.
4) Rebuild; if it succeeds, remove src/emit/irgen.mmt, src/emit/irgen.nan,
   src/emit/irgen.issue and continue to rerunning all tests.
